   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "Research, groups, and studies that exist",
   "text": "The National Tay-Sachs & Allied Diseases Association is a US patient group that the atlas links to work on Sandhoff disease [E01216c0]. The Cure and Action for Tay-Sachs (CATS) Foundation is a UK-based patient group that also supports families affected by Sandhoff disease [Ec45768c]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a natural history study called 'Natural History of Glycosphingolipid Storage Disorders and Glycoprotein Disorders' is recruiting in the United States and studies Sandhoff disease [Ea158c9f, Ed665e20]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a study called 'UCB Transplant of Inherited Metabolic Diseases With Administration of Intrathecal UCB Derived Oligodendrocyte-Like Cells' is recruiting in the United States for Sandhoff disease [Eb6761e2, Ec109198]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a not-yet-recruiting trial testing PLX-200 is planned for Sandhoff disease [E516f6f2, E0fb2a07]. According to ClinicalTrials.gov, a gene therapy study for GM2 gangliosidosis, which includes Sandhoff disease, is planned to take place in France [E081011a, E7735499]. The National Tay-Sachs & Allied Diseases Association also runs a natural history study called PRONTO and a Variant (Mutation) Database, both linked to Sandhoff disease [E48e5738, E5debefc]. According to NIH RePORTER, grants such as 'Mouse Models of Novel Sphingolipid Biology and Disease Mechanisms' and 'Pathogenesis Informs Therapy for Glycosphingolipid and Glycoprotein Disorders' study Sandhoff disease [Ec7665cc, Ec9638f7]. Researchers Richard Proia and Cynthia Tifft are listed as the people leading some of these funded grants connected to Sandhoff disease [E5894b74, E20732b2]. For Tay-Sachs, a biologically similar disease, there is also a large phase 3 trial of an oral medicine called Nizubaglustat recruiting in many countries [E05ee7b4, Ef8b116b].",
